{"repositoryId":288822892,"availability":"available","full":"o-inha/PaintingStoner","name":"PaintingStoner","description":"Webapp for optimizing projector guided painting.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2020-08-19T19:47:45Z","updated":"2026-09-25T09:24:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["art","fader","image-transformation","painting","projection","projector-control","projector-guided-painting","webapp"],"demo":"https://inha.asia/dmo/painting-stoner","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:40.250Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:40.250Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:40.250Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T19:33:40.250Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["(Note that the fading animation is much smoother in reality than in this 4 frames per second gif.)","Painting Stoner is a simple browser-based tool for optimizing projector guided painting. I.e. when you use a real-life projector to project a digital image on your real-life canvas for real-life painting, whether you use projecting for making a rough sketch, learning perspectives or even attempting to paint the projected image.","I developed this tool for my own purposes after purchasing a $50 projector for sketching initial perspectives more accurately. All features are built around that cheap-ass projector's shortcomings as well as otherwise making many aspects of the process significantly more convenient."],"features":["Free perspective transformation of image. This enables you to keystone the image to your canvas despite the projector position or what kind of keystoning features it has. Optional guidelines are present for more…","Extended opacity control with animated auto-fading. In addition to basic opacity slider, the Stoner includes an opacity range slider where you can select two opacity values. You can easily switch between these values…","Mul